{{Quote|Saleucami has fallen, and Master Vos has moved his troops to Boz Pity.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]|<ref name="ROTS" />}}
The '''Siege of Saleucami''' was one of the longest campaigns of the [[Outer Rim Sieges]] during the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] on the [[planet]] [[Saleucami]]. The siege lasted for five [[Standard month|months]] and saw the deployment of [[Oppo Rancisis's legion]], [[Quinlan Vos's legion]], and the [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]], all of which opposed a large [[Saleucami force|Separatist defense force]]. In the end, the Republic managed to defeat [[Confederacy military|Separatist forces]]. Afterward, Vos' [[legion]] left for [[Boz Pity]], [[Stass Allie]] was [[Death|killed]] with the enactment of [[Order 66]] whilst patrolling Saleucami with [[clone trooper]]s.

==Prelude==
During the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the sleepy [[planet]] of [[Saleucami]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] grew to become a major site of conflict, even being branded as one of the [[Triad of Evil]].<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> When [[General]] [[Grievous]] sought control of the world, it began a [[Battle of Saleucami|battle]] between the Republic and Separatists.<ref name="Grievous Intrigue">{{TCW|Grievous Intrigue}}</ref><ref name="The Deserter">{{TCW|The Deserter}}</ref> When it seemed as though Saleucami could return to its peaceful status, [[Separatist officer|Confederate strategists]] realized it could be used as a trans-shipment base for the [[Foundry of the Confederacy]],<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> launching an [[invasion of Saleucami]] that brought widespread fighting to the planet.<ref name="Collapse" /> The Confederacy established a large [[Saleucami force|force]] on Saleucami and a [[blockade]] of [[starship]]s in [[orbit]].<ref name="Scarif and Other Planets" />

==The siege==
{{Quote|Oh, and please forgive the delay, but since my transfer to Saleucami, my free moments (which I can then also use to support your progress) have been rather scarce.|Commander Neyo|<ref name="OSWM 121">{{GermanFanCite|121|Database}}</ref>}}
During the [[Outer Rim Sieges]], fighting broke out between the Republic and the Separatists on Saleucami<ref name="HC 33">{{HelmetCollectionCite|33|Helmets}}</ref> when [[Republic Intelligence]] feared it was being used to hide Separatist secrets, with possibilities including a [[Unidentified clone-soldier program|Separatist clone-soldier program]], [[superweapon]] development, and work in the field of [[biological warfare]] with engineered plagues. The Confederacy's<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> campaign to defend Saleucami was one of the longest of the sieges<ref name="HC 33" /> at five months long.<ref name="DB 122" /> During the battle, Republic forces faced guerilla attacks.<ref name="OSWM 123">{{GermanFanCite|123|Database}}</ref>

[[Jedi General]] [[Oppo Rancisis]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Quinlan Vos]], his [[troop]]s,<ref name="ROTS" /> Jedi General [[Stass Allie]], and her<ref name="BC 33" /> [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]] besieged the planet.<ref name="Force Collection Neyo Light" /> By the time of the [[Battle of Coruscant]], the Republic had nearly won the battle.<ref name="OSWM 123" /> Eventually, the Republic was able to defeat the [[Confederacy military|Separatist forces]],<ref name="ROTS" /> capturing the planet for the Republic.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==Aftermath==
{{Quote|Troops should be pulling their forces, not securing a post. The war is over.|[[Hunter]], a clone deserter|<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>}}
[[File:BARCspeeder_DB.png|thumb|left|250px|The 91st Recon Corps patrols the swamplands after the battle's formal ending.]]
Once Saleucami had fallen, Vos moved his forces to [[Boz Pity]], leaving Stass Allie<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> and the 91st to mop up the remains of the [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]]. However, while patrolling the world's [[swamp]]lands on [[speeder bike]]s with Allie, [[Clone Commander]] [[Neyo]] received [[Order 66]] from [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]. This caused his genetically implanted [[behavioral modification biochip]] to activate, forcing him and his [[Wingmate|wingman]] to open fire on Allie, [[Death|killing]] her.<ref name="ROTS" />

Following the siege,<ref name="ROTS" /> even after the war itself had finished, the clone troopers remained on Saleucami instead of pulling out, enforcing the control of the newly-established [[Galactic Empire]]. Saleucami citizens found themselves forced to register for [[chain code]]s and had their [[starship]]s taken away by [[Clone impound vessel|impound vessels]]. In order to get offworld on a ship, citizens needed to register for a chain code, which clone deserter [[Cut Lawquane]]&mdash;who had been warned by deserting [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] that Saleucami was no longer a safe place to hide&mdash;learned while trying to get offworld with [[Lawquane family|his family]]. Nevertheless, with the help of fellow deserters [[Clone Force 99]], the Lawquanes secured fake chain codes, allowing them to leave the planet aboard a [[Star Commuter 2000]].<ref name="Cut and Run" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Commander-on-Saleucami.png|thumb|right|300px|A Clone Commander leads forces on Saleucami]]
The Siege of Saleucami was first referenced in ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="ROTS" /> Within the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the events surrounding the battle were expanded upon in ''[[Star Wars: Republic: Siege of Saleucami]]'', the eighteenth story arc of [[Dark Horse Comics]]' ''[[Star Wars: Republic]]'' series.<ref name="Republic 74">[[Republic 74|''Republic'' 74]]</ref> The "Clone Commander" card art from the ''[[Republic Specialists Personnel Expansion]]'',<ref name="Clone Commander">{{Legion|set=Republic Specialists Personnel Expansion|cardname=Clone Commander (Personnel)}}</ref> art that was first teased in the "Standing Out" article on [[Fantasy Flight Games]]'s website,<ref name="Standing Out">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2021/1/6/standing-out|text=Standing Out}}</ref> featured a [[Clone Commander]] commanding clones on Saleucami during the era of [[Phase II clone trooper armor]].<ref name="Clone Commander" /> It is unclear if the battle depicted is meant to be the Siege of Saleucami.

According to "[[Yoda and Other Users of the Force]]," Stass Allie only took part in the mop-up operations after the Siege of Saleucami, arriving after the [[Battle of Coruscant]] with reinforcements meant for the [[Battle of Felucia (Outer Rim Sieges)|Battle of Felucia]], only for her and her troopers to be rerouted to Saleucami.<ref name="YaOUotF">{{EncyclopediaCite|Yoda and Other Users of the Force}}</ref> However, the majority of sources list her as taking part in the battle proper.<ref name="BC 33" /><ref name="Force Collection Neyo Light" /><ref name="TCW" /> As such, this article assumes "Yoda and Other Users of the Force" is incorrect.

In the non-canon [[LEGO Star Wars|LEGO ''Star Wars'']] television series ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Freemaker Adventures|The Freemaker Adventures]]'', the B1 battle droid [[R0-GR]] revealed he fought in the siege. Speaking with [[Wick Cooper]], R0-GR claimed to have only gotten through the five month long battle by drinking [[30-weight motor oil]].<ref name="Zander's Joyride">{{FreemakerAdventures|Zander's Joyride}}</ref>

